# PDF Deck Button Naming

When adding a `<Button>` or `<a>` that links to a PDF deck, the label **must** follow this pattern:

```
"Deck - [Topic the deck addresses]"
```

## Examples

✅ GOOD
```jsx
<Button label="Deck - Genie Best Practices" link={useBaseUrl('/pdfs/Genie Best Practices.pdf')} />
<Button label="Deck - UC Best Practices" link={useBaseUrl('/pdfs/UC Best Practices.pdf')} />
<Button label="Deck - Metric Views" link={useBaseUrl('/pdfs/UC-Metric-Views.pdf')} />
```

❌ BAD
```jsx
<Button label="UC Best Practices Deck" ... />
<Button label="View PDF" ... />
<Button label="Genie Spaces Implementation Guide" ... />
```

## Placement

- Place deck buttons inside a `:::tip` admonition (never `:::warning` or `:::danger`).
- Add a short lead-in sentence before the button, e.g. "For a more elaborated explanation, check the following deck:"
